@@ -127,6 +127,24 @@ debouncedSave('data2'); // This will run after the first save completes
 //=> Saved: data2
 ```
 
+#### clearQueue(reason?)
+
+Type: `Function`
+
+Only available on the function returned by `pDebounce.promise()`. With `after: true`, discards the invocation queued while the current invocation is running and rejects all promises waiting for it. The function returns the number of waiting calls discarded, not the number of function executions. A queued invocation that has started running is not affected.
+
+If `reason` is omitted or `undefined`, the discarded promises reject with an error whose name is `AbortError`. Other values, including `null`, `false`, and `0`, are used as the exact rejection reason.
+
+```js
+const pendingSave = debouncedSave('latest');
+
+if (shouldCancel) {
+	console.log(debouncedSave.clearQueue()); //=> 1
+}
+```
+
+With the default `after: false`, calls share the active promise rather than queueing another invocation, so `clearQueue()` returns `0` and does not cancel the active call.
+
